system "BSI:chu-Cyrl:Latn:1958" {

metadata {
  authority_id bsi
  id 1958
  language iso-639-2:chu
  source_script Cyrl
  destination_script Latn
  name "BS 2979:1958 Transliteration of Cyrillic and Greek characters - Table D, Transliteration of Church Slavonic Cyrillic"
  url https://www.bsigroup.com
  creation_date 1958
  confirmation_date 2000-05
  description {    BS 2979:1958, Table D: transliteration of Church Slavonic Cyrillic. The table
    covers the full Church Slavonic alphabet including the yuses, ksi, psi, fita
    and izhitsa, with the letters' numerical values annotated.
  }

  notes {
    note "The digraph-letter pairs и and й are given as glyph variants in one row: и is romanized i with macron (long i) and the breve-marked variant й as i with breve (short i); likewise i and the diaeresis-marked variant (i-krataya glyph) are romanized i and i with diaeresis."
    note "The Church Slavonic yus series: little yus e with ogonek, big yus o with ogonek, iotated little yus j plus e-ogonek, iotated big yus j plus o-ogonek; the iotated-e glyph je and the iotated-a digraph ja."
    note "Omega is romanized o with macron. The digraph uk (o plus u, with the monograph-uk glyphs as variants) is romanized u with macron, the table also showing the alternative rendering as the two separate letters."
    note "Fita is romanized f with dot above (distinguishing it from ef); izhitsa is romanized y with dot above."
    note "Shcha is romanized s-caron plus t in this table. The hard sign is romanized u with breve (the table's footnote: it occurs only after consonants), and yery is romanized y."
    note "The numerical-value column of the source annotates the letters used as numerals (a=1, v=2, g=3, d=4, e=5, dze=6, z=7, i=8, i=10, k=20, l=30, m=40, n=50, o=70, p=80, r=100, s=200, t=300, uk=400, f=500, kh=600, psi=700, omega=800, ts=900, ch=90, ksi=60, fita=9, izhitsa with the thousands sign); the footnote describes the titlo, the diaeresis marking thousands, and the thousands-sign constructions for 10000 and over. This map renders the letters, not the numeral values."
    note "Transcribed visually from the scanned table page of the digitized BS 2979:1958 (BSI 05-2000 reprint); the fita and izhitsa cells were confirmed at 20x magnification."
  }
}

